finding. The second plot's surface-38-moss-234 association is not a viability certificate. When the examination cannot resolve viability, new growth or propagation, report unknown explicitly. Retain exact plot, processId, remaining inspection rounds, exposure and paid effort across interruption; resume revalidates access and pays only outstanding work. Explicit cancel or death settles the lock once without automatically covering exposed material or refunding spent energy/time. Cancellation does not convert the planted root into inventory. Existing specimen ageing continues while unattended, including while exposed; disclose the physical disturbance and exposure risk without inventing a risk probability. Completed evidence and physical changes persist. No passive assessment, tending effect, automatic reinspection or maintenance benefit is created. Further examination requires another actual paid action. Personal evidence is shared only through actual communication; other participants must act independently. Development/review waiting advances no world time. Established checks, accounting, progress and evidence limitations execute in the existing code, not repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Assessment, learning, requests, naming and reaching an observation interval do not themselves earn pleasure or satisfaction. Repeated unchanged findings earn no information-gain benefit. A genuinely informative observed change or informative negative result may be considered only by the existing single grounded-understanding/evidence-deduplicated rule, with personal applicability, its existing bounded amount, cap, decay and cooldown; this reuse adds no reward rule or separate reward for the same evidence. An unsupported or inconclusive query alone is not verified information gain. No comfort, nutrition, health or energy restoration is supplied. Protected reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions remain unchanged.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Keep functional evidence distinct from presentation and experience. Reuse the actual root plot's plant component and existing appearance; use observable work events and retained exposure/progress to distinguish examination begun, uncovered, interrupted, covered and completed findings. Evidence metadata should reference the target ID, processId, tick, method, completed stage and supported finding or unknown status so it can be reused without implying a new physical effect. A covered plot or completed inspection must not display germination, a viable-plant badge, food, propagation or a successful diagnosis unsupported by observation. Failed access produces no examination-success event; interrupted inspection may show only the exposure and work actually completed. Public visuals disclose only observable physical events, not Moss's private report or concealed specimen properties.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"4547678b-690f-44bb-96fd-ee7ee3b7b92d","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"mediu